const faqs: [string, string][] = [
  ["What’s the difference between PHP and IOP?", "PHP is more intensive, about six hours a day, Monday through Friday. IOP is lighter (around three hours, four days), so you can keep working or going to school. Many clients step down from PHP into <a class='inl' href='/programs/intensive-outpatient-program/'>IOP</a> as they stabilize."],
  ["Do I stay overnight?", "No, PHP is a day program. You receive intensive care during the day and go home each night to sleep in your own bed."],
  ["How many hours a day is PHP?", "About six structured hours a day, Monday through Friday, 9 AM–3 PM."],
  ["Can I customize my schedule?", "Yes, one of the unique features of our PHP is a customizable approach that lets you build a tailored schedule for the group component, choosing the groups best aligned with your goals."],
  ["Do you offer an addiction PHP?", "Yes. Our addiction PHP in Glastonbury stabilizes symptoms of substance use and co-occurring disorders through evidence-based modalities, individualized plans, and specialized interventions, including <a class='inl' href='/treatment-methods/medication-assisted-treatment/'>MAT</a> for opioid and alcohol dependence."],
