  ["Is PHP the same as inpatient treatment?", "No. You sleep at home. If you need 24-hour care or are in immediate danger, call or text 988, call 911, or go to the nearest emergency room."],
  ["Can I work while in PHP?", "Most people take time off work or school during PHP because it runs most of the day. Ask our admissions team about leave paperwork; see <a class='inl' href='/post/what-programs-at-hopewell-are-eligible-for-ct-paid-leave-or-fmla/'>which programs are eligible for CT Paid Leave or FMLA</a>."],
  ["Will my insurance cover it?", "Most commercial plans cover PHP when it’s medically necessary. We’ll <a class='inl' href='/rates-and-insurance-coverage/'>verify your benefits for free</a>, in minutes. Hopewell does not accept Medicare or Medicaid (HUSKY); if that’s your coverage, our team can point you to programs that take it."],
  ["Do I need a referral for PHP?", "You can call us directly, and we also accept referrals from hospitals, doctors and therapists. Our <a class='inl' href='/admissions/'>admissions team</a> will tell you if your plan requires one."],
  ["What happens after PHP?", "Most people step down to IOP, then to <a class='inl' href='/programs/counseling/'>counseling</a> and <a class='inl' href='/programs/medication-management/'>medication management</a> with the same team."],
